# No create-and-wait CDP loops

Agents verifying this Blogger/theme project must not hang on create → wait cycles.

## Hard rules

1. **Reuse tabs** — `browser_tabs` list first; reuse `viewId`. Do not open a new tab or `start_remote_daemon` when one already works.
2. **No long CDP polls** — Never `Runtime.evaluate` with `setTimeout` / `Promise` waits >300ms (no toast polling). Use one sync evaluate (`awaitPromise: false`) returning all fields needed.
3. **One shot** — Batch pin/version/DOM reads in a single evaluate. Ban chains: create → wait → create → wait.
4. **Click/snapshot first** — Prefer `browser_click` / `browser_mouse_click_xy` / `browser_snapshot`. CDP only when snapshot cannot answer.
5. **Blogger Save** — After 1–2 failed Save automations, stop polling; ask user to click Lưu once; then one fast sync check.
6. **CDN bumps** — Do not invent a new `_bump_cdn_*.py` + wait-for-jsDelivr loop every turn when one bump + one verify is enough.

## Bad vs good

```js
// BAD — hangs 1.5–8s inside MCP→CDP every call
(() => new Promise(r => setTimeout(() => r({saved:/Đã lưu/.test(document.body.innerText)}), 1500)))()

// GOOD — sync, one round-trip
(() => {
  const v = document.querySelector('.CodeMirror')?.CodeMirror?.getValue() || '';
  return { n: (v.match(/v2026\.11\.13\.\d+/g)||[]).length, clean: !!document.querySelector('.CodeMirror')?.CodeMirror?.isClean?.() };
})()
```
